A||||7||WKDFIRO||New MR2 - A KILL!!!!||||6||
Z||000000||WKDFIRO||08-29-2000||09:49 PM||||So I was on my way to the freeway when from a side street come a brand new red MR2 with its top up and tinted windows. We come to the red light and I hear him actually rev up and "toe" the crosswalk line. I thought I would be the jerk and stick my head out the window and make like I was trying to hear his revs. Then I let out a roar from my 2.8 blueprinted, cam'd, 2.5 inch exhaust with no muffler 85 GT. <BR>     On went the green light and off I went walking away from him! I could hear the engine winding way out when I was just getting the second wind out of second. He obviously didn't know the car yet because he bogged it off the line. We came up to the stop sign in front of us and I let the engine wind down in second just trumpeting the pipes. He got the jump on my this time because he must have wound it up to around 5 grand before he dumped it. I took off after him and not only caught up with him at 3 grand on my tach but kept going past him. We parted ways from there but all I could think of was: <P>WAIT TILL I TELL THE FORUM ABOUT THIS!!!!!<P>The 2's engine could not have been broken in yet, the driver probably raced it for the first time on me. But it was nice to whomp on some Toyota tin again!<P>You guys with the 3.4 should have even MORE fun with these things! ||||reg||6
Z||000001||JohnnyK||08-30-2000||02:20 AM||||If you mean a new 2000 MR2, yeah, those things only have about 140 HP or so. But if we are talking about a '91+ (I think) turbo'd, we don't stand a chance.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mattsfiero||08-30-2000||08:00 AM||||Never say that Johnny ...You saw the cars at Kick hill there are very few Stock 2.5's aroud and alot have the Modifications some adding up to an extra 50-to as much as 100 HP to the cars...Those little wanna b Fieros lack the handling and ability that our fieros do and don't stand a chance<P>Matt||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||08-30-2000||03:07 PM||||I just mean we would lose if it was a stock 2.5 or 2.8, as they have 60 hp over the 2.8. I would assume the stock MR2 handling (after 92 though) would be better than a stock Fiero. Mind you, there are a lot more modifications for the Fiero to bring it up to par.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||08-30-2000||05:12 PM||||The new MR2's are screaming for the 180 HP Yamaha engines out of the Celica GTS's.  That engine would move the little roadster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Its good to see that the Fiero can take the new 2's!  Great kill!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mattsfiero||08-30-2000||10:19 PM||||Well think about it they have what 50 HP over the 2.8 okay I can see that but if you look at it they are made out of what compared to a Fiero....You got it Metal ..there over all weight is almost 2,000lbs over the fiero and I will tell you that makes a big diference where it counts...(Also I believe they are still using Power assited sterring lowering the handling verses a fiero's manual steering)<P>Matt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||08-30-2000||10:35 PM||||The MR2s have ALWAYS been lighter than the Fiero despite being made of metal. The space frame on the Fiero has always pushed it to almost 3000 lbs. The MR-2s have the power too. BUT look closely at where it is at! Top end power both in hp and most important in a stop light race, in torque. The Fiero has always had the low end grunt on the Toys. Thats why we have to get them off the line   as soon as we can because when the Toy finally hit the upstairs rpm than it gets interesting.<P>I wouldn't think that a moderately built 3.4 with headers would have any problems even with the 170 hp MR2 that are inevitable.||||reg||14
Z||000007||fiero56||08-30-2000||11:04 PM||||Interesting concept, a 5,000 pound MR2. What is that, the same weight as a new Ford Excursion. The newest MR2 weighs in around 2,100lbs. Fiero weighs 2,500-2,900.||||reg||1
